bg3le component meta: walk a LegacyMap/LegacyRefMap again at entry 0, so a read never reuses a walk of freed nodes

On top of 0001-0011. legacy_map_node kept one walk per thread, reused while the map's address and item count
were unchanged. When an entry is replaced (one removed, another added: same count), the kept walk still names
the removed node, which the game has freed. v010 live windows 8-9 (ops/logs/live.md, runtime/probes/v010w8-w9):
Ext.Utils.GetDialogManager().Dialogs listed key 214 (an ended automated dialog) with DialogId -91782656
(0xFA878000, freed memory) and Dialogs[215] nil, while the party's DialogState.DialogId was 215, and a raw walk
of the same map (Peek, no cache) in the same kind of load found exactly one entry, key 215, whose instance reads
DialogId 215. Guard.lua's dialogue_info reads the same map on every action (Bench B3: an instance reading
DialogId 0 and a building mesh as its resource after the dialogue ended).

- Every read of such a map starts at entry 0 (the Lua key scan `for i = 0, count - 1`, a value by its slot
  `[i]`), so entry 0 now rebuilds the walk; entries 1..n of the same pass reuse it (still linear).

Offline: tools/test_bg3le_legacy_map_walk.py compiles legacy_map_node from the patched source against a fake
map and replaces its one entry at the same count. Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0011. Applied by
tools/build_bg3le.sh.
